      }
    ],
    "status": "present",
    "value": "If both groups have equal averages, each equals the overall average. Replace each value x by n*x - total; now the overall average is 0 and the question becomes whether some non-empty proper subset sums to 0 (its complement then also sums to 0). Split the array into two halves and list all subset sums of each. A zero-sum subset is either a non-empty subset of one half (excluding the full array) or a combination of a non-empty subset of the right half with a subset of the left half whose sum is the negation. To keep the subset proper, the left part used with the full right half cannot also be the full left half."
  },
